-13_Madeira_122_Funchal%2C_Hafen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cathedral of Funchal","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.648333,"lo":-16.908333,"d":591,"ds":"The Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption (Portuguese: Sé Catedral de Nossa Senhora da Assunção) is a Catholic cathedral in Sé, Funchal, Madeira, Portugal, serving as the mother church of the Diocese of Funchal, which encompasses all of the Autonomous Region of Madeira. Completed in 1514, it is one of the few structures that survives virtually intact since the early period of colonization of Madeira.","wpu":"Cathedral of Funchal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Catedral%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-29%2C_DD_34.jpg/960px-Catedral%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-29%2C_DD_34.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"British Cemetery of Funchal","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.648889,"lo":-16.916389,"d":681,"ds":"The British Cemetery of Funchal is on the Portuguese island of Madeira.","wpu":"British Cemetery of Funchal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Sketches_of_Funchal%2C_Madeira_-_The_English_Cemetery%2C_ILN_1866.jpg/960px-Sketches_of_Funchal%2C_Madeira_-_The_English_Cemetery%2C_ILN_1866.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Raid on Ruhnu (1917)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.65,"lo":-16.916667,"d":797,"ds":"The Raid on Ruhnu on 15 June 1917 was a minor operation proceeded by Imperial German Naval Air Forces in Ruhnu Island in the Gulf of Riga during World War I. Several German seaplanes landed on the coast of Ruhnu to attack the Russian telegraph station and after that retreated to their home base, which is considered as the first air-landing ambush operation in the military history.","wpu":"Raid on Ruhnu (1917)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/German_seaplanes_land_on_the_Russian_island_of_Ruhnu_to_destroy_the_radio_station%2C_15_June%2C_1917.png/960px-German_seaplanes_land_on_the_Russian_island_of_Ruhnu_to_destroy_the_radio_station%2C_15_June%2C_1917.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Convent of Santa Clara (Funchal)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.651241,"lo":-16.913401,"d":815,"ds":"The Convent of Santa Clara is a convent of clarisses in Funchal, Madeira, Portugal. It was built on the late 15th century to house the daughters of nobility in the island. The convent was developed around a primitive church, church of Nossa Senhora da Conceição de Cima, ordered by João Gonçalves Zarco, the island's discover and first donatary captain of Funchal, to be his family tomb.","wpu":"Convent of Santa Clara (Funchal)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Monastery_of_Santa_Clara_in_Funchal.jpg/960px-Monastery_of_Santa_Clara_in_Funchal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Mercado dos Lavradores","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.648639,"lo":-16.903889,"d":918,"ds":"The Mercado dos Lavradores (English: farmers' market) is a fruit, vegetable, flower and fish market in Funchal, Madeira. The building was designed by Edmundo Tavares and opened on 24 November 1940. The facade, main entrance and fish market contain traditional Azulejo (panels of tiles) depicting regional themes, executed by João Rodrigues.","wpu":"Mercado dos Lavradores","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Mercado_dos_Lavradores.jpg/960px-Mercado_dos_Lavradores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Capela do Corpo Santo","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.647639,"lo":-16.9,"d":1194,"ds":"The Capela do Corpo Santo or Chapel of Corpo Santo is a 15th century chapel at the end of the old village of Funchal (Rua D. Carlos I 64, 9060-051 Funchal, Portugal). It is dedicated to the patron saint of fishermen, Saint Pedro Gonçalves Telmo, the \"Corpo Santo\". It is decorated with ceiling paintings, gilded carved wood altars, and sculptures in the Manueline style.","wpu":"Capela do Corpo Santo","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Capela_do_Corpo_Santo.jpg/960px-Capela_do_Corpo_Santo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Belmond Reid's Palace","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.640556,"lo":-16.924167,"d":1201,"ds":"Belmond Reid's Palace (a.k.a. Reid's Palace) is a historic hotel located to the west of Funchal Bay in Madeira, Portugal, in an imposing position looking out over the Atlantic Ocean. The hotel has sloping gardens.","wpu":"Belmond Reid's Palace","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Funchal%2C_Reid%E2%80%99s_Palace_%28from_Ribeiro_Seco%29.jpg/960px-Funchal%2C_Reid%E2%80%99s_Palace_%28from_Ribeiro_Seco%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Fort of São Tiago","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.646667,"lo":-16.898583,"d":1290,"ds":"The Fort of São Tiago (Portuguese: Fortaleza de São Tiago) is a historic military fort located in the historical centre (Zona Velha) of Funchal, Madeira. Constructed in the early 17th century, the fort was built to protect the island against pirate attacks and foreign invasions.","wpu":"Fort of São Tiago","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Funchal%2C_Praia_de_S%C3%A3o_Tiago.jpg/960px-Funchal%2C_Praia_de_S%C3%A3o_Tiago.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Funchal Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.642,"lo":-16.8953,"d":1579,"ds":"Funchal Bay is a large bay opposite the main city of Funchal on the island of Madeira, located in the North Atlantic Ocean off the west coast of Morocco in north Africa. Funchal has its harbour located within the bay. Belmond Reid's Palace is located on the headland at the western end of the bay.","wpu":"Funchal Bay","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/Ba%C3%ADa_do_Funchal_vista_de_Este_-_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Jewish cemetery, Funchal","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.647409,"lo":-16.894911,"d":1644,"ds":"The Jewish Cemetery of Funchal is a Jewish cemetery located in Rua do Lazareto, Funchal, Madeira. Sephardi Jews as well as Ashkenazi Jews are buried here.","wpu":"Jewish cemetery, Funchal","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cemit%C3%A9rio_Judaico%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal.jpg/960px-Cemit%C3%A9rio_Judaico%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Quinta da Boa Vista (Madeira)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.653073,"lo":-16.896291,"d":1783,"ds":"The Quinta da Boa Vista is a historic quinta ('estate') and orchid garden in the Santa Maria Maior parish of Funchal on the island of Madeira, overlooking the central and western parts of Funchal. It contains one of the last remaining walled stair terrace gardens of Funchal and continues to draw its water from the levada irrigation system.","wpu":"Quinta da Boa Vista (Madeira)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/View_from_the_Quinta_da_Boa_Vista.jpg/960px-View_from_the_Quinta_da_Boa_Vista.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"João Gomes Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.663,"lo":-16.898,"d":2486,"ds":"João Gomes Bridge (Portuguese: Ponte João Gomes) is a bridge in Funchal, the capital city of the Portuguese island of Madeira. It forms part of the VR1, Madeira. It was completed in 1994 and was designed by engineer António José Luís dos Reis.","wpu":"João Gomes Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Ponte_Jo%C3%A3o_Gomes.jpg/960px-Ponte_Jo%C3%A3o_Gomes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Madeira Botanical Garden","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.6622,"lo":-16.8958,"d":2528,"ds":"Madeira Botanical Garden (Portuguese: Jardim Botânico da Madeira) is a botanical garden in Funchal, Madeira, opened to the public in 1960. The area was previously part of an estate belonging to the family of William Reid, founder of Reid's Hotel.","wpu":"Madeira Botanical Garden","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Jardim_Bot%C3%A2nico_da_Madeira_01.jpg/960px-Jardim_Bot%C3%A2nico_da_Madeira_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Igreja de São Martinho","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.649139,"lo":-16.943972,"d":3047,"ds":"The Church of St Martin (Portuguese: Igreja de São Martinho) is the main church in the Freguesia (Parish in English) of São Martinho (Funchal), Madeira. Dedicated to St. Martin of Tours.","wpu":"Igreja de São Martinho","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Iglesia_de_San_Mart%C3%ADn%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-29%2C_DD_47.jpg/960px-Iglesia_de_San_Mart%C3%ADn%2C_Funchal%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-29%2C_DD_47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church of Our Lady of the Mount","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.676,"lo":-16.9025,"d":3667,"ds":"The Church of Our Lady of the Mount (Portuguese: Igreja de Nossa Senhora do Monte) is the main church in the civil parish of Monte, in Funchal, Madeira island.","wpu":"Church of Our Lady of the Mount","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Nossa_Senhora_do_Monte.jpg/960px-Nossa_Senhora_do_Monte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Praia Formosa","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.641667,"lo":-16.954444,"d":3982,"ds":"The Praia Formosa is a beach on the Portuguese island of Madeira. It is the fashionable district of Funchal and a popular beach location. Famous residents include Christopher Columbus, Merche Romero, and Cristiano Ronaldo.","wpu":"Praia Formosa","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Polovina_Praia_Formosa.JPG/960px-Polovina_Praia_Formosa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Christ the King (Madeira)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.6386,"lo":-16.8507,"d":5771,"ds":"The Christ the King statue (Portuguese: Cristo Rei) also known as the Sacred Heart statue, is an Art Deco statue of Jesus Christ in Garajau, Madeira.","wpu":"Christ the King (Madeira)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/XrystosSpasytelGarajau.JPG/960px-XrystosSpasytelGarajau.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Garajau","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.633333,"lo":-16.85,"d":5925,"ds":"The Garajau Partial Nature Reserve is a Portuguese marine reserve located on the Funchal Bay offshore Madeira Island. The protected area has existed since 1986. It is a location for snorkelling and scuba-diving.","wpu":"Garajau","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Erizo_de_mar_viol%C3%A1ceo_%28Sphaerechinus_granularis%29%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-31%2C_DD_40.jpg/960px-Erizo_de_mar_viol%C3%A1ceo_%28Sphaerechinus_granularis%29%2C_Madeira%2C_Portugal%2C_2019-05-31%2C_DD_40.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Farol de Câmara de Lobos","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.647,"lo":-16.975639,"d":5967,"ds":"The Farol de Câmara de Lobos is a small lighthouse on the south coast of the island of Madeira, Portugal. The lighthouse was built in 1937 on top of a promontory at a focal height of 23 metres, and is located about 7 km west of the city of Funchal.","wpu":"Farol de Câmara de Lobos","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/C%C3%A2mara_de_Lobos_-_Portugal_%28271229776%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Cabo Girão","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":32.656389,"lo":-17.006667,"d":8969,"ds":"Cabo Girão (European Portuguese pronunciation: [ˈkaβu ʒiˈɾɐ̃w]) is a lofty sea cliff located along the southern coast of the island of Madeira, in the Portuguese archipelago of Madeira, geographically part of Africa. Cabo Girão is a tourist lookout point, with up to 1800 visitors a day. The location is also a common starting point for hikers.","wpu":"Cabo Girão","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Base_of_Cabo_Girao_from_viewpoint_2013.JPG/960px-Base_of_Cabo_Girao_from_viewpoint_2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Madeira, officially the Autonomous Region of Madeira, is an autonomous region of Portugal, in the Atlantic Ocean about 805 km (500 miles) southwest of mainland Portugal. Together with the Azores, it is one of the two autonomous regions of Portugal and a special territory of the European Union. It is the southernmost point and region of Portugal.","wpu":"Madeira","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Flag_of_Madeira.svg/960px-Flag_of_Madeira.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}